From: TactiQ OS BSP <bsp@tactiqedge.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rk3588s-rock-5a: reserve a ramoops area

pstore/ram needs a fixed physical area that a warm reset does not clear.
Without it CONFIG_PSTORE_RAM has no backend and /sys/fs/pstore stays empty.

Address chosen against the running board rather than by convention:

  /proc/iomem      System RAM 0x00200000-0xefffffff, reserved regions at
                   0x03ea0000-0x041affff, 0xe8ebf000-0xeced3fff (swiotlb,
                   DTB) and 0xee000000-0xefffffff (CMA)
  U-Boot env       kernel_addr_r 0x02000000, pxefile_addr_r 0x00e00000,
                   fdt_addr_r 0x12000000, ramdisk_addr_r 0x12180000

0x18000000 sits above every address the bootloader writes to and below
every region the kernel reserves, so neither overwrites the records
between the failing boot and the boot that reads them.

Layout of the 1 MiB area: 256 KiB of console output and the remainder as
128 KiB panic records. The console region is the larger consumer on
purpose: the cause of a failed boot is in the lines before the panic, not
in the panic itself.

no-map is deliberately not set. The region must stay in the kernel linear
map so pstore reaches it through memremap; marking it no-map forces an
ioremap mapping whose unaligned accesses fault on arm64.

This applies on top of 0002, which leaves the file at 873 lines.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [TactiQ BSP integration - board-specific
 memory reservation; not intended for mainline submission]
Signed-off-by: TactiQ OS BSP <bsp@tactiqedge.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-rock-5a.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-rock-5a.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-rock-5a.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-rock-5a.dts
@@ -871,3 +871,18 @@
 		spi-max-frequency = <1000000>;
 	};
 };
+
+/ {
+	reserved-memory {
+		#address-cells = <2>;
+		#size-cells = <2>;
+		ranges;
+
+		ramoops@18000000 {
+			compatible = "ramoops";
+			reg = <0x0 0x18000000 0x0 0x00100000>;
+			console-size = <0x00040000>;
+			record-size = <0x00020000>;
+		};
+	};
+};
